  "details": "In situations with high OSC traffic, such as when using facial tracking, OSC messages that notify parameter changes from `VRCAvatarParameterDriver` may be dropped.\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. Switch avatar to `avtr_df4b0f6c-fa42-4ad5-8ccd-26ab94ccffcd`.\n\nThis avatar has parameters `Counter` and `Recv[0-15]`, where `Counter` is incremented every frame by `VRCAvatarParameterDriver`.\n\n2. Launch a program that receives `Counter` while continuously updating `Recv[0-15]`.\n\nSource code: https://gist.github.com/logicmachine/4aea8bf071461f01cfa38b20e3b912b2\n\nThis program outputs the received `Counter` values while sending OSC messages that update `Recv[0-15]` at 100Hz intervals.\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n\nThe `Counter` values should be output as consecutive values in sequence.\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\n\nThe output `Counter` values have gaps/are non-consecutive.\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nBased on packet capture analysis, the messages are not being sent out, suggesting this is a transmission-side issue rather than a reception-side problem.\n\nAdditionally, parameters manually controlled through the ExpressionsMenu appear to be less likely to be dropped.",
